RESOLUTION OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF [COMPANY NAME] (PRO-FORMA FIRST BOARD RESOLUTION)

WHEREAS, the shareholders of [Company Name], a wholly foreign-owned enterprise duly formed as a limited liability company under the Company Law of the People's Republic of China, have caused the Company to be registered and have duly appointed the undersigned directors to constitute the initial Board of Directors; and

WHEREAS, the Articles of Association of the Company authorize the Board of Directors to exercise all powers necessary to organize and conduct the Company's business, provide for the subscription and payment of share capital, open bank accounts, adopt a registered office, and appoint statutory officers;

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED, subject to applicable law and the Articles of Association, as follows:

1. SHARE CAPITAL SUBSCRIPTION AND ALLOTMENT. IT IS RESOLVED that the issued and paid-up share capital of the Company shall be established in accordance with the registered capital stated in the Articles of Association; the Board confirms the subscription of all registered capital by the sole shareholder; the Board records the in-kind or monetary contribution plan; the Board directs the Chief Financial Officer to procure the capital contribution verification report if required by local practice; and to file the completed capital contribution information in the national enterprise credit information publicity system within the prescribed period;

2. BANKING AUTHORIZATIONS. IT IS RESOLVED that the legal representative and/or the finance director, either singly or jointly as determined by the Board, be and are hereby authorized to negotiate and execute all account opening mandates, facility letters, loan and trade finance documents, and electronic banking agreements with local commercial banks; that such bank accounts shall include the basic deposit account as well as general and foreign currency accounts; and that the authorized signatories shall have signing authority consistent with the financial authority matrix approved by the Board;

3. ADOPTION OF REGISTERED OFFICE. IT IS RESOLVED that the premises located at [registered address] be and are hereby adopted as the Company's registered office in China for all statutory purposes; that lease documents, property ownership certifications and utility contracts be approved; and that the management be directed to notify the Administration for Market Regulation and the tax authority of any future change of registered office in strict compliance with the registration procedures;

4. APPOINTMENT OF STATUTORY OFFICERS. IT IS RESOLVED THAT [Name] be appointed as the legal representative; [Name] as director and general manager; [Name] as supervisor; and [Name] as the person in charge of the company's licensed operations and compliance officer; that the supervisor shall not simultaneously serve as a director or senior manager; that the appointments take effect immediately; and that each officer provide all necessary signatures for filings with SAMR, the tax authority, customs, the social insurance bureau and the civil defense and environmental licensing authorities;

5. GENERAL ADMINISTRATION. IT IS RESOLVED that the Board, through management, shall prepare and affix the company seal, the finance seal and the legal representative seal in accordance with PRC practice and shall adopt an internal seal-use register; that the directors shall cause the completion of the foreign investment filing with MOFCOM and the reporting of final beneficial owners in the national information platform; and that expenditure incidental to incorporation, licensing and licensing renewals be approved and ratified;

6. GOVERNANCE AND SEVERABILITY. IT IS RESOLVED that the Board shall establish an audit and compliance committee where required by regulatory risk-based rules, and shall hold at least one board meeting per annum with proper minutes; and hereby resolves that each paragraph shall be severable and enforceable independently to the extent permitted by law.

All the foregoing resolutions were proposed, seconded, and adopted by unanimous vote of the directors present and constituting quorum. There being no further business, the meeting was adjourned.

[Place] [Date] [Signature Block: Director Secretary]
